# C++ standards

C++20 floor (`std: 23` only when the catalog row says so). C++ Core Guidelines. Details: [docs/style.md](docs/style.md).

```cpp
// BAD
auto* p = new double[n];
// ...
delete[] p;

// GOOD — ownership in the type
std::vector<double> x(n);
std::span<double> view{x};
```

- No bare `new`/`delete`. No `using namespace std;` in headers.
- Non-owning views: `std::span` / `std::string_view`, not raw pointers to someone else’s buffer.
- `const` by default. Encode ownership in signatures.
- Headers in `toolbox/include/toolbox/` are included as `#include <toolbox/name.hpp>`, `#pragma once`, self-contained.
- Lesson code sits between `// start <id>` and `// end <id>` for Sphinx.
- Identifiers: `snake_case` functions and variables, `PascalCase` types. Files and folders stay kebab-case.
- Prefer the standard library. A third-party dependency must be pinned and justified in the leaf README.
